1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You

2
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:13,100
Don't you think it's a little too hot to be wearing all of that kick kick we've gone over this before heirs of the night tribe

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,600
We're not affected by heat the way mortals are oh

4
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,480
Jeez, it's like walking into a hairdryer. Oh

5
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,480
Oh

6
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:28,240
Detestable light of the Sun

7
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:36,080
You have won today's battle, but there shall come a time when the night tribe will fill up the world in darkness and then no more light

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Right now I wouldn't object to that

9
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:25,163
I'm still alive.

10
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:28,023
Big brother, you must be exhausted.

11
00:02:28,583 --> 00:02:30,423
So nice of you to join us today.

12
00:02:31,163 --> 00:02:33,523
Yeah, just like I always do at this time.

13
00:02:34,043 --> 00:02:35,143
It's summer vacation.

14
00:02:35,303 --> 00:02:37,283
Why would you wait until school would normally be out?

15
00:02:38,623 --> 00:02:40,203
What time did you guys get here?

16
00:02:40,403 --> 00:02:41,263
About one o'clock.

17
00:02:41,943 --> 00:02:43,443
Meat was already here being productive,

18
00:02:43,443 --> 00:02:45,023
playing a video game.

19
00:02:45,183 --> 00:02:46,323
She wasn't that far in.

20
00:02:46,443 --> 00:02:48,243
Yozra showed up just a little after Senna.

21
00:02:48,623 --> 00:02:49,483
So early.

22
00:02:49,683 --> 00:02:51,443
And let me guess, you were here too.

23
00:02:51,623 --> 00:02:53,003
I arrived here at 8 a.m.

24
00:02:53,163 --> 00:02:55,603
It was very important for me to be here before you.

25
00:02:55,703 --> 00:02:57,523
I'd rather take my own life than have you wait.

26
00:02:57,643 --> 00:03:00,203
Don't take this the wrong way, but it's not that big a deal.

27
00:03:01,183 --> 00:03:02,823
I've already prepared your lunch.

28
00:03:03,583 --> 00:03:05,703
Uh, that's sweet, but I ate before I left.

29
00:03:06,063 --> 00:03:08,183
I'm sorry, and there's no reason to cook for me

30
00:03:08,183 --> 00:03:09,123
now that school's out.

31
00:03:09,663 --> 00:03:12,023
Does this mean my services are no longer needed

32
00:03:12,023 --> 00:03:13,023
and you're letting me go?

33
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:14,703
Heaven help my heart.

34
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,783
My big brother doesn't need me anymore.

35
00:03:17,243 --> 00:03:18,643
I am worthless in his eyes.

36
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:20,763
I have no choice but to end it all.

37
00:03:20,963 --> 00:03:22,323
I didn't mean it like that.

38
00:03:22,363 --> 00:03:22,863
I need you.

39
00:03:22,923 --> 00:03:23,823
I'm just not hungry.

40
00:03:23,923 --> 00:03:25,403
If you're not going to eat both of those,

41
00:03:25,503 --> 00:03:26,203
can I have one?

42
00:03:26,243 --> 00:03:26,883
I'm starving.

43
00:03:27,203 --> 00:03:27,403
Ugh.

44
00:03:28,163 --> 00:03:29,063
Brilliant timing.

45
00:03:29,443 --> 00:03:31,483
I bet she was expecting me to bring her something.

46
00:03:32,983 --> 00:03:34,143
Look, you saved the day.

47
00:03:34,463 --> 00:03:36,163
Is it cool if I give this to Maria instead?

48
00:03:36,603 --> 00:03:37,763
Not that I wouldn't want it.

49
00:03:37,903 --> 00:03:39,803
I just mean it would help if you made her lunch

50
00:03:39,803 --> 00:03:42,003
instead of me during the summer break to save time.

51
00:03:42,003 --> 00:03:44,583
Um, it would not be appropriate for a samurai

52
00:03:44,583 --> 00:03:45,683
to serve two masters.

53
00:03:45,883 --> 00:03:46,343
I'm sorry.

54
00:03:46,723 --> 00:03:48,123
What is he talking about?

55
00:03:48,543 --> 00:03:49,463
All right, listen.

56
00:03:49,723 --> 00:03:51,243
It's not serving two masters.

57
00:03:51,703 --> 00:03:52,843
Maria's like a sister to me,

58
00:03:52,903 --> 00:03:54,843
so you'd be doing a noble service for your master

59
00:03:54,843 --> 00:03:56,483
if you looked after her, wouldn't you?

60
00:03:57,443 --> 00:03:58,343
Yes, I would.

61
00:03:58,343 --> 00:03:59,303
You're right.

62
00:03:59,963 --> 00:04:02,263
I would actually consider it a great honor, sir.

63
00:04:02,843 --> 00:04:03,843
You mean it?

64
00:04:04,543 --> 00:04:06,183
You see me as your little sister?

65
00:04:07,983 --> 00:04:08,823
Miss Maria,

66
00:04:09,003 --> 00:04:10,943
my big brother has requested

67
00:04:10,943 --> 00:04:12,423
that I prepare your meals for you,

68
00:04:12,523 --> 00:04:14,303
and so I will now be at your service.

69
00:04:14,543 --> 00:04:15,023
I know!

70
00:04:15,243 --> 00:04:16,003
Isn't it great?

71
00:04:16,223 --> 00:04:16,443
Yeah!

72
00:04:17,443 --> 00:04:17,843
Oh!

73
00:04:18,403 --> 00:04:20,583
You got all this stuff from the convenience store?

74
00:04:21,103 --> 00:04:23,043
Oh, look how much sugar's in them!

75
00:04:23,043 --> 00:04:23,543
Yum!

76
00:04:27,843 --> 00:04:28,243
Yum!

77
00:04:28,423 --> 00:04:30,043
Yeah, this isn't the healthiest meal

78
00:04:30,043 --> 00:04:30,883
you could have brought me.

79
00:04:31,163 --> 00:04:32,623
You're such a strong, healthy man.

80
00:04:32,743 --> 00:04:33,743
I knew you could handle it.

81
00:04:33,803 --> 00:04:34,843
Plus, you deserved a break.

82
00:04:35,043 --> 00:04:35,563
Thank you.

83
00:04:35,723 --> 00:04:36,783
Let's say from here on out

84
00:04:36,783 --> 00:04:39,163
you prepare only nutritious meals for Maria, okay?

85
00:04:39,503 --> 00:04:40,223
I understand.

86
00:04:40,383 --> 00:04:40,983
As you wish.

87
00:04:41,163 --> 00:04:42,603
What's the point in learning good behavior

88
00:04:42,603 --> 00:04:44,243
if you're just going to give the reward away?

89
00:04:44,243 --> 00:04:53,183
See you later.

90
00:04:53,343 --> 00:04:54,003
Have a good day.

91
00:04:59,123 --> 00:04:59,963
Oh, man.

92
00:05:00,283 --> 00:05:00,823
Made it.

93
00:05:01,083 --> 00:05:01,823
Good to see you.

94
00:05:01,883 --> 00:05:03,323
Looks like you've already been working hard.

95
00:05:03,683 --> 00:05:04,003
Hi.

96
00:05:04,083 --> 00:05:04,763
Where is everyone?

97
00:05:05,383 --> 00:05:05,923
I don't know.

98
00:05:06,063 --> 00:05:06,823
They're not here yet.

99
00:05:07,283 --> 00:05:08,843
Miss Maria came by for a little while

100
00:05:08,843 --> 00:05:10,843
and then remembered she had some sisterly duties

101
00:05:10,843 --> 00:05:12,203
to tend to, so she went home.

102
00:05:12,763 --> 00:05:13,123
Okay.

103
00:05:13,123 --> 00:05:14,763
Did you bring her lunch?

104
00:05:15,103 --> 00:05:15,463
Yes.

105
00:05:15,743 --> 00:05:16,903
I made sure it was healthy

106
00:05:16,903 --> 00:05:17,983
just as you instructed.

107
00:05:18,283 --> 00:05:20,063
Very rich in vitamins and calcium.

108
00:05:20,243 --> 00:05:20,923
And protein.

109
00:05:22,003 --> 00:05:24,103
How many protein shakes did she drink?

110
00:05:24,163 --> 00:05:25,743
It wasn't easy to tell you the truth.

111
00:05:25,863 --> 00:05:27,303
She resisted, but they were your order,

112
00:05:27,443 --> 00:05:29,163
so I had no choice but to force them down.

113
00:05:29,663 --> 00:05:30,743
Tell me you're joking.

114
00:05:31,243 --> 00:05:32,963
It reminded me a little of that story

115
00:05:32,963 --> 00:05:34,163
we learned in history class

116
00:05:34,163 --> 00:05:36,063
about the execution of Mampuku Maru.

117
00:05:36,523 --> 00:05:37,263
Mampuku who?

118
00:05:37,723 --> 00:05:38,143
Maru.

119
00:05:38,263 --> 00:05:40,223
He was only ten when his parents abandoned him

120
00:05:40,223 --> 00:05:42,043
thinking he'd be safe from the evil rulers.

121
00:05:42,043 --> 00:05:43,723
Instead, he was found and beheaded.

122
00:05:44,303 --> 00:05:45,963
I bet the way that little boy screamed

123
00:05:45,963 --> 00:05:46,783
when he met his death

124
00:05:46,783 --> 00:05:48,183
sounded just like poor Maria.

125
00:05:48,523 --> 00:05:49,623
What do you mean, scream?

126
00:05:49,963 --> 00:05:51,443
Please, tell me what happened.

127
00:05:52,103 --> 00:05:53,823
She resisted, but they were your order,

128
00:05:53,943 --> 00:05:55,683
so I had no choice but to force them down.

129
00:05:56,203 --> 00:05:57,143
Your orders.

130
00:05:57,583 --> 00:05:58,463
Your orders.

131
00:05:58,943 --> 00:05:59,723
Your orders.

132
00:05:59,723 --> 00:06:04,003
All right, starting tomorrow,

133
00:06:04,143 --> 00:06:05,143
see if you can make something

134
00:06:05,143 --> 00:06:06,623
that's both nutritious and tastes good

135
00:06:06,623 --> 00:06:07,403
to a ten-year-old.

136
00:06:07,683 --> 00:06:10,103
I don't need any more Mampukuru incidents here.

137
00:06:10,483 --> 00:06:10,803
Right.

138
00:06:11,223 --> 00:06:12,403
Your wish is my command.

139
00:06:19,983 --> 00:06:21,183
Oh, man.

140
00:06:21,183 --> 00:06:24,303
Are they ever going to show up?

141
00:06:24,683 --> 00:06:26,323
You've had such a long day, big brother.

142
00:06:31,603 --> 00:06:33,363
You're all here, of course.

143
00:06:33,863 --> 00:06:35,363
Why didn't any of you come yesterday?

144
00:06:36,243 --> 00:06:37,123
Poor Kodaka.

145
00:06:37,363 --> 00:06:39,363
Were you feeling lonely by yourself without Rika?

146
00:06:40,003 --> 00:06:42,343
Lonely is not exactly the word I would use.

147
00:06:42,563 --> 00:06:43,243
Sorry, Kodaka.

148
00:06:43,363 --> 00:06:44,563
Something suddenly came up.

149
00:06:45,003 --> 00:06:46,923
Yeah, and I was too busy being jerked around.

150
00:06:47,363 --> 00:06:47,983
How so?

151
00:06:48,683 --> 00:06:50,343
I thought the game was almost over,

152
00:06:50,443 --> 00:06:52,363
so I was just going to finish it and then leave.

153
00:06:52,483 --> 00:06:53,403
But as it turns out,

154
00:06:53,423 --> 00:06:54,943
I actually had four more hours to go,

155
00:06:55,043 --> 00:06:56,163
way longer than I expected.

156
00:06:56,663 --> 00:06:58,343
I didn't even notice what time it was

157
00:06:58,343 --> 00:06:59,703
because I was lost in the journey.

158
00:06:59,963 --> 00:07:01,883
When Makane finally met her prince at the end,

159
00:07:01,923 --> 00:07:03,543
it was so beautiful, I couldn't move.

160
00:07:05,723 --> 00:07:07,403
You were playing a video game.

161
00:07:07,863 --> 00:07:08,963
It's more than just a game.

162
00:07:09,023 --> 00:07:09,683
You can borrow it.

163
00:07:09,703 --> 00:07:10,143
You'll see.

164
00:07:10,383 --> 00:07:11,863
It's a life-changing experience.

165
00:07:12,503 --> 00:07:14,063
When you finish, you have to start it over.

166
00:07:14,063 --> 00:07:16,043
The ending changes the entire meaning of the beginning

167
00:07:16,043 --> 00:07:16,823
and the whole journey,

168
00:07:16,823 --> 00:07:18,243
you just wouldn't realize it's about how we're all in a...

169
00:07:18,243 --> 00:07:19,383
I just thought of something.

170
00:07:19,683 --> 00:07:19,983
What?

171
00:07:21,003 --> 00:07:23,203
Let's come up with a way that we can let each other know

172
00:07:23,203 --> 00:07:24,683
what time we're all going to be here

173
00:07:24,683 --> 00:07:25,863
and if we can make it or not.

174
00:07:26,063 --> 00:07:27,683
I think you may be onto something there.

175
00:07:27,943 --> 00:07:30,063
I'm surprised that came out of you, Kodaka.

176
00:07:30,663 --> 00:07:32,703
But now that it has, how do we do it?

177
00:07:32,863 --> 00:07:35,883
I was thinking maybe like an internet group or something?

178
00:07:35,923 --> 00:07:36,623
You're crazy.

179
00:07:36,903 --> 00:07:38,143
You won't even consider it?

180
00:07:38,323 --> 00:07:40,403
I try to use the internet as little as possible.

181
00:07:40,603 --> 00:07:42,703
Online shopping and research are about it for me.

182
00:07:42,783 --> 00:07:43,623
Okay, but why?

183
00:07:43,623 --> 00:07:45,303
I did something recently

184
00:07:45,303 --> 00:07:47,043
and I don't want to be recognized.

185
00:07:48,043 --> 00:07:49,923
I'm not even going to ask what that's about.

186
00:07:50,103 --> 00:07:51,023
I appreciate it.

187
00:07:51,343 --> 00:07:53,643
Yeah, I had a pretty crappy experience with message boards

188
00:07:53,643 --> 00:07:55,543
so I'm not interested in being found online.

189
00:07:55,923 --> 00:07:57,943
Just thinking about it pisses me off.

190
00:07:58,143 --> 00:08:00,323
I could kill those ugly trolls for the way they treated me.

191
00:08:00,403 --> 00:08:02,463
They will never be forgiven for the things they said.

192
00:08:03,183 --> 00:08:03,823
What happened?

193
00:08:03,883 --> 00:08:04,783
Did you get in a fight?

194
00:08:05,283 --> 00:08:06,283
I was harassed.

195
00:08:06,323 --> 00:08:08,683
They were calling Natsumi a heartless, lobotomized hooker

196
00:08:08,683 --> 00:08:09,983
just because of the way she looks

197
00:08:09,983 --> 00:08:11,663
and I was not going to let that slide.

198
00:08:11,663 --> 00:08:13,143
I told them looks aren't everything

199
00:08:13,143 --> 00:08:15,423
and she's actually very nice once you get to know her.

200
00:08:15,583 --> 00:08:16,963
And how well do you know her?

201
00:08:17,143 --> 00:08:19,263
Well enough that talking crap about her around me

202
00:08:19,263 --> 00:08:21,043
is pretty much a declaration of war.

203
00:08:21,423 --> 00:08:24,043
They can either admit they were wrong and apologize to me

204
00:08:24,043 --> 00:08:25,303
or we can fight it out

205
00:08:25,303 --> 00:08:27,263
and determine who's right the old-fashioned way.

206
00:08:27,723 --> 00:08:29,463
So what you're saying is message boards

207
00:08:29,463 --> 00:08:30,643
aren't going to work for you, right?

208
00:08:31,003 --> 00:08:31,763
Oh, I know.

209
00:08:32,203 --> 00:08:35,163
How about setting up a page for a private group on Nixie?

210
00:08:35,703 --> 00:08:37,603
What are you doing on Nixie, Kodaka?

211
00:08:37,963 --> 00:08:39,443
And why haven't you added me?

212
00:08:39,443 --> 00:08:41,483
Because I'm not on it, that's why.

213
00:08:41,963 --> 00:08:42,483
You know it?

214
00:08:42,803 --> 00:08:43,143
Yeah.

215
00:08:43,423 --> 00:08:44,623
You're a member, aren't you?

216
00:08:44,843 --> 00:08:45,623
Of course not.

217
00:08:45,683 --> 00:08:47,763
Why would I put myself out there for all those stalkers?

218
00:08:47,883 --> 00:08:48,743
Yeah, I agree.

219
00:08:49,223 --> 00:08:50,783
Rika's not a member yet either.

220
00:08:51,283 --> 00:08:53,263
Turns out it's not the easiest site to join.

221
00:08:53,363 --> 00:08:54,623
You have to actually know someone

222
00:08:54,623 --> 00:08:56,383
and have them add you to their contact list.

223
00:08:57,183 --> 00:08:58,763
So since none of us are members,

224
00:08:58,863 --> 00:09:00,283
we couldn't join if we wanted to.

225
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:03,063
Nixie isn't the only social networking site, though.

226
00:09:03,263 --> 00:09:04,543
There must be something private

227
00:09:04,543 --> 00:09:06,003
that doesn't require an invitation.

228
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:07,623
Rika has a suggestion.

229
00:09:08,623 --> 00:09:10,643
Why don't we just exchange phone numbers

230
00:09:10,643 --> 00:09:11,743
and use text messaging?

231
00:09:13,743 --> 00:09:14,183
Texting?

232
00:09:14,703 --> 00:09:17,023
You mean send messages with our cell phones?

233
00:09:17,343 --> 00:09:18,983
Yeah, that's what it is, right?

234
00:09:19,763 --> 00:09:20,643
I guess.

235
00:09:21,103 --> 00:09:22,363
I mean, I forget sometimes

236
00:09:22,363 --> 00:09:24,103
I can text people besides my sister.

237
00:09:24,843 --> 00:09:26,163
Rika, you are a genius!

238
00:09:26,663 --> 00:09:27,323
Text messaging?

239
00:09:27,603 --> 00:09:29,123
I never even thought about that.

240
00:09:29,483 --> 00:09:31,143
The only other thing I used on my phone

241
00:09:31,143 --> 00:09:33,463
was the GPS in some karaoke apps they downloaded.

242
00:09:34,063 --> 00:09:34,903
That does it.

243
00:09:35,403 --> 00:09:36,843
Rika, you leave me no other option

244
00:09:36,843 --> 00:09:38,243
but to agree that you are a genius.

245
00:09:38,603 --> 00:09:40,363
Rika is very thankful for the compliments.

246
00:09:40,883 --> 00:09:42,343
Okay, great, let's do this!

247
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:44,323
Who's ready to exchange numbers with Rika?

248
00:09:45,063 --> 00:09:45,783
I am.

249
00:09:49,203 --> 00:09:50,443
Okay, here it is.

250
00:09:55,183 --> 00:09:56,163
I'll go get mine.

251
00:09:56,163 --> 00:10:01,583
Come on.

252
00:10:01,803 --> 00:10:02,403
Here it is.

253
00:10:02,743 --> 00:10:04,403
This is my cellular telephone.

254
00:10:06,023 --> 00:10:08,523
The numbers don't just jump in there by themselves.

255
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:10,223
Oh, yeah, that's a good point.

256
00:10:10,603 --> 00:10:12,203
Rika's never seen one like this.

257
00:10:12,283 --> 00:10:13,123
It's so pretty.

258
00:10:13,363 --> 00:10:14,783
The color almost glows.

259
00:10:15,243 --> 00:10:16,243
Uh, thank you?

260
00:10:16,243 --> 00:10:16,283
Thank you.

261
00:10:26,163 --> 00:10:30,443
Rika sent a group text.

262
00:10:30,523 --> 00:10:31,243
Did you all get it?

263
00:10:31,443 --> 00:10:32,743
You messaged all of us?

264
00:10:33,023 --> 00:10:34,123
I don't have anything.

265
00:10:34,223 --> 00:10:35,103
You sure you sent it?

266
00:10:35,303 --> 00:10:36,603
I didn't get anything either.

267
00:10:36,983 --> 00:10:38,243
Maybe my phone doesn't get them?

268
00:10:38,463 --> 00:10:40,063
Or maybe you have to send it to me separately.

269
00:10:40,623 --> 00:10:41,803
Where would I look for it?

270
00:10:41,903 --> 00:10:43,183
Which picture do I click on?

271
00:10:43,343 --> 00:10:44,623
I'm not seeing anything.

272
00:10:45,283 --> 00:10:47,083
Rika, you might have to send it to me again.

273
00:10:47,163 --> 00:10:47,563
This sucks!

